  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 900 PM EDT Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Isolated-scattered showers possible overnight, but the \nthreat for severe WX or flooding is low. \n\nLatest Wx analysis shows that the cold front now generally S of\nthe region, with earlier showers/storms mainly confined to\ncentral and southern NC. There are some additional showers over\nmoving in from the north, but they are spotty and PoPs through\nthe late evening and overnight have been lowered to 20-30% or\nless. Some patchy fog/low stratus may develop after midnight,\nwith the guidance generally favoring the piedmont. Overnight\nlows will mostly range from the upper 60s to around 70F, with\nsome mid 60s in the piedmont, and locally staying in the lower\n70s near the coast in SE VA/NE NC. Shower/storm chances are\nfairly low Sun (15-35% PoPs) with most convection likely confined\nto the far southern portions of the area (or remaining south altogether).\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Relatively cooler temperatures are expected \nearly next week with a brief warmup by Wed/Thu.\n\nBeyond Sun, dry conditions are expected early next week, likely\ncontinuing into midweek. The next chance of rain appears to \narrive on Thursday or Friday ahead of a cold front, though \nguidance is not overly optimistic regarding this.",
